# ML Core layer for Linux x86_64
# Target-owned lockfile for deterministic pip-compile resolution.
#
# This file is Linux-specific because pip-compile cannot resolve
# conditional dependencies across platforms in a single graph.
#
# Run `make compile-ml-linux-x86_64` in this directory to generate pinned ml-core-linux.txt
#
# PLATFORM TARGETS:
#   - linux-x86_64-cpu    (Linux Intel/AMD, CPU baseline)
#   - linux-x86_64-cuda   (Linux Intel/AMD, NVIDIA GPU)
#
# SECURITY NOTE:
#   This Linux lock is retained only as a frozen historical manifest.
#   weights_only=True remains mandatory defense in depth for all checkpoint
#   loads.
#
# See: requirements/README.md for layering rationale.

# --- PyTorch (Linux frozen historical baseline) ---
torch==2.8.0  # Frozen historical pin
torchvision==0.23.0  # Frozen historical companion pin

# Diffusion / HuggingFace ecosystem
# Keep transformers<5 while the managed inference surface remains on 4.57.x.
diffusers>=0.36.0,<1
transformers>=4.57.0,<5
huggingface-hub>=0.19.0,<2
accelerate>=0.20.0,<2

# Vision / segmentation helpers (cross-platform)
controlnet-aux>=0.0.6,<1
efficientsam==1.0.0          # Deterministic builds: stable EfficientSAM weights
open-clip-torch==3.3.0       # Deterministic builds: SAM2/CLIP stack compatibility

